course: dictionary
lesson: 11566
title: A word from Scotland and a chemistry ending
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one place or one subject. «Ane» is a Scots word, and you may meet it in old Scottish poems and songs, such as those by Robert Burns. In Scots, «ane» means «one».
explain: «Ane o them is my best pal.» Ask yourself: what word would fit here? One of them means one of the group, so ane must mean one. Swap in one to check: «One o them is my best pal» still makes sense.
explain: You may also see «-ane» at the end of some science words. It is a chemistry ending, and it is not a word you can use alone. «Butane» and «propane» are two gases used as fuels. When a word is a fragment like this, it helps to check a dictionary.
fact: «Ane» is a Scots word meaning «one».
fact: As a word on its own, «ane» is not standard English.
fact: Robert Burns was a famous Scottish poet who wrote in Scots, so you may meet «ane» in his work.
fact: The ending «-ane» is used in chemistry names of some gases and fuels, such as «methane», «propane», «butane» and «octane».
fact: A fragment is a small part of a word, and it does not always mean something by itself.
exercise: «Ane o them is my best pal.» In Scots, what does ane mean? | Two | Lost | *One | Happy
exercise: Which word ends with the chemistry ending -ane? | *Propane | Puddle | Planet
exercise: Is «ane» a normal word you would find in standard English on its own? | Yes, it is a common word in every English story | *No, on its own it is not standard English | Only in Australia | Only in London
test: «Butane is a gas used in some lighters.» What does the ending -ane tell you about butane? | A type of fruit | It is a Scottish greeting | It is a sound a cat makes | *It is a chemistry name for some gases and fuels
test: «Ane o the lads won the race.» What does ane mean in this sentence? | Fast | Three | Winner | *One
exam: Which of these is a fuel name ending in -ane? | Orange | Ladder | *Octane | Ankle
